 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 506975,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "What is the sum of the first 101 terms of an arithmetic sequence with <span data-math=\"{a_1} = 13\">{a_1} = 13</span>  and <span data-math=\"d = 2.25\">d = 2.25</span>?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The sum of the first <span data-math=\"n\"></span> terms of an arithmetic sequence is: <span data-math=\"{s_n} = n\\left({\\frac{{{a_1} + {a_n}}}{2}} \\right)\"></span>.</p>\n<p>You do not know the last term, so first use <span data-math=\"{a_i} = {a_1} + d \\times \\left({i - 1} \\right)\"></span> to find the 101st term.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"{a_{101}} = 13 + 2.25 \\times \\left({101 - 1} \\right) = 13 + 2.25(100) = 13 + 225 = 238\"></span></p>\n<p>Now, you can use the sum formula.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"{s_n} = 101\\left({\\frac{{13 + 238}}{2}} \\right) = 101\\left({\\frac{{251}}{2}} \\right) = 12,675.5\"></span></p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "12,675.5"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
